From: Winter21c <winter@localhost>
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-xiaomi-raphael: instantiate the second CCI controller

The ultrawide module (stock DT `qcom,cam-sensor@3`, CAMU_*) is on **CCI1 master0**
(i2c@ac4b000), but the single `cci@ac4a000` node with the sm8250-compatible
binding exposes only CCI0's two masters (`/dev/i2c-3`, `/dev/i2c-4`), because
`drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c` has `NUM_MASTERS 2` and maps
`i2c-bus@<n>` to `cci->master[n]`.

Adding a second node is clean: the driver only ever uses **reg index 0** and
**IRQ index 0** (`devm_platform_get_and_ioremap_resource(pdev, 0, ...)` and
`platform_get_irq(pdev, 0)`), so it never touches `cci_top`/`cci1` from the first
node's reg list and there is no overlapping mem-region claim.  The new node
therefore takes just its own 4 KiB window at 0xac4b000 and SPI 271, and exposes
CCI1's masters as additional adapters - the ultrawide sits on CCI1 master0.

Not tested yet: the phone was wedged while this was written (round 21).

Signed-off-by: Winter21c <winter@localhost>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
@@
 	cci: cci@ac4a000 {
 		compatible = "qcom,sm8250-cci";
 		reg = <0x0 0x0ac4a000 0x0 0x1000>,
 		      <0x0 0x0ac4b000 0x0 0x1000>,
 		      <0x0 0x0ac4e000 0x0 0x1000>;
 		reg-names = "cci0", "cci1", "cci_top";
@@
 			};
 		};
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * Second CCI controller.  The driver above maps only reg index 0, so it
+	 * never claims 0xac4b000 itself; a separate node with its own 4 KiB
+	 * window and its own IRQ is the way to reach CCI1 master0, where the
+	 * ultrawide (S5K3L6) lives.
+	 */
+	cci1: cci@ac4b000 {
+		compatible = "qcom,sm8250-cci";
+		reg = <0x0 0x0ac4b000 0x0 0x1000>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 271 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+		power-domains = <&camcc TITAN_TOP_GDSC>;
+		#address-cells = <1>;
+		#size-cells = <0>;
+		status = "okay";
+
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&cci1_default>;
+
+		i2c-bus@0 {
+			reg = <0>;
+			clock-frequency = <400000>;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+
+			/* ultrawide S5K3L6: address has to be discovered by
+			 * scanning this bus once it is registered */
+		};
+	};
